Drive Darwin native compilation with runtime-discovered options.

The statically linked libgccjit bakes the build machine's SDK path into
the compiled driver, and linking an .eln needs the GCC runtime archives
(libemutls_w.a and friends) that upstream expects next to an installed
GCC.  Inject the required driver options at compile time instead:

  -isysroot <xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path>
      so a downloaded Emacs.app native-compiles against whatever SDK is
      active on the running machine, surviving Xcode moves and upgrades;

  -L<Emacs.app>/Contents/Frameworks/libgccjit -static-libgcc
      so the driver links .eln files against the runtime archives
      bundled inside the app, keeping it relocatable.

The options are appended to the compilation context rather than to the
`native-comp-driver-options' defcustom: a user setq of that variable
must not be able to strip flags the build depends on.

--- a/lisp/emacs-lisp/comp.el
+++ b/lisp/emacs-lisp/comp.el
@@ -3317,6 +3317,25 @@
   "Compile as native code the current context naming it NAME.
 Prepare every function for final compilation and drive the C back-end."
   (let ((dir (file-name-directory name)))
+    ;; With the statically linked libgccjit, the driver needs options
+    ;; naming the active SDK and the GCC runtime archives bundled inside
+    ;; Emacs.app.  GCC bakes the build machine's SDK path into libgccjit;
+    ;; query xcrun for the SDK on the running machine instead, so a
+    ;; downloaded app keeps native-compiling after Xcode moves or is
+    ;; upgraded.  The bundled runtime directory provides libemutls_w.a
+    ;; and friends for linking .eln files; locate it relative to the
+    ;; Emacs binary so the app stays relocatable.
+    (when (eq system-type 'darwin)
+      (let ((default-directory invocation-directory))
+        (setf (comp-ctxt-driver-options comp-ctxt)
+              (append
+               (list "-isysroot"
+                     (car (process-lines "/usr/bin/xcrun" "--sdk" "macosx"
+                                         "--show-sdk-path"))
+                     (concat "-L" (expand-file-name "../Frameworks/libgccjit"
+                                                    invocation-directory))
+                     "-static-libgcc")
+               (comp-ctxt-driver-options comp-ctxt)))))
     (comp--finalize-relocs)
     (maphash (lambda (_ f)
                (comp--log-func f 1))
